    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36906" root="كرنب" body-key="k">
    
      Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كرنب</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَرْنَبَةٌ</span>, <i>He fed</i> a guest
<i>with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَرْنِيب</span>. (K.) Ex. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَرْنِبُوا لِضَيْفِكُمْ فَإِنَّهُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَتَْحَانُ</span> <i>Feed your guest with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كرنيب</span>, <i>for he is
hungry.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, <i>He ate</i> [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كرنيب</span>, or]
<i>dates with milk.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  AHei and others assert
the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ن</span> to be augmentative; but in the T, L, and
K it is implied that it is radical. (MF.)

